To initialize the IDF GPIO on an ESP32, you can use the following function:

```c
void initialize_idf_gpio(void) {
    // Include the necessary header
    #include "driver/gpio.h"

    // Initialize the GPIO
    gpio_config_t io_conf;
    io_conf.intr_type = GPIO_INTR_DISABLE;
    io_conf.mode = GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT;
    io_conf.pin_bit_mask = (1ULL << GPIO_NUM_0); // Change GPIO_NUM_0 to your desired GPIO
    io_conf.pull_down_en = GPIO_PULLDOWN_DISABLE;
    io_conf.pull_up_en = GPIO_PULLUP_DISABLE;
    gpio_config(&io_conf);
}
```

This function configures GPIO 0 as an output. You can change `GPIO_NUM_0` to any other GPIO number you wish to configure.
